%%% note
HTTP/2 で受けた要求の payload は、Content-Type に関係なく */* (Binary) になる (実 Mule 4.11.3。HTTP/1.1 は Content-Type の形式)。
DW は as String で読める。output の無い式の出力形式の推論は式ごとに最初の 1 回だけなので、最初に HTTP/2 の要求で評価した
sizeOf(payload as String) は Java の数になり、後の HTTP/1.1 の要求でも数のまま。
%%% port 18575
%%% request POST /mime h2=1
Content-Type: application/json; charset=UTF-8

{"a": 1}
%%% response 200
content-type: application/json; charset=UTF-8

{
  "mimeType": "*/*",
  "text": "{\"a\": 1}",
  "contentType": "application/json; charset=UTF-8",
  "version": "HTTP/2"
}
%%% request POST /mime
Content-Type: text/plain

hello
%%% response 200
content-type: application/json; charset=UTF-8

{
  "mimeType": "text/plain",
  "text": "hello",
  "contentType": "text/plain",
  "version": "HTTP/1.1"
}
%%% request POST /mime h2=1
Content-Type: text/plain

hello
%%% response 200
content-type: application/json; charset=UTF-8

{
  "mimeType": "*/*",
  "text": "hello",
  "contentType": "text/plain",
  "version": "HTTP/2"
}
%%% request POST /infer h2=1
Content-Type: text/plain

0123456789
%%% response 200
content-type: application/json; charset=UTF-8

{
  "n": 10,
  "mimeType": "application/java"
}
%%% request POST /infer
Content-Type: text/plain

0123456789
%%% response 200
content-type: application/json; charset=UTF-8

{
  "n": 10,
  "mimeType": "application/java"
}
